-- title:
--   The two branches of X₁(Mp) above A: count and degrees
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M\ne 0$ with $5\le M$ and $p\nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((q))$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the ratios of $q$-expansions of integral forms of equal weight on $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $p\in\mathfrak m_A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $\varpi$ a generator of $\mathfrak m_A$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\subseteq L\subseteq K$. Let $j\in K$, non-zero, have image in $L((q))$ the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $=q^{-1}\cdot(\text{integral } j\text{-numerator})$, and let $w$ be an `IntegralWeightOneForm` over $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ of level $M$: a weight-one form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with an integral power series realising its $q$-expansion and having non-zero image in $\kappa((q))$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ characterised by: $f\in W_0$ iff $f\cdot y=x$ in $L((q))$ for some $x,y\in A[[q]]$ with $y$ of non-zero reduction modulo $\mathfrak m_A$. Finally let $\sigma$ be an $L$-automorphism of $K$ sending $j$ to the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.qExpand ℚ p`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25) applied to [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (substitution $q\mapsto q^p$), such that the pullback $\sigma^{-1}W_0$ differs from $W_0$ and contains $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ for every $P\in A[X]$ with non-zero reduction. Four assertions follow. First, every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ containing the image of $A$, with $\mathfrak m_A$ mapping into the non-units of $V$, and containing $P(j)^{\pm 1}$ for every $P\in A[X]$ of non-zero reduction, equals $W_0$ or $\sigma^{-1}W_0$. Second, for every such $V$ and every non-unit $f$ of $V$ there is $g\in V$ with $f=\varpi g$. Third, if $R_0$ is an intermediate field of $\kappa\subseteq\kappa((q))$ whose elements are exactly the quotients $\bar x/\bar y$ arising from the above presentations $f\cdot y=x$ of elements $f$ of $W_0$, then the relative degree `IntermediateField.relfinrank` of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC κ M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) in $R_0$ is $p-1$. Fourth, the relative degree of the coefficientwise base change to $L$ of the $q$-expansion field of $\Gamma_1(M)$ in $K$ is $p^2-1$ (natural subtraction throughout).
--
--   This is the $e\cdot f$ table for the two branches of the special fibre of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[\zeta_p]$ lying above the generic point of the $j$-line: the branch through the cusp $\infty$, whose Gauss reduction field is the Igusa field of relative degree $p-1$ over $\kappa(X_1(M))$, and its companion obtained from $j\mapsto j(q^p)$, with no others and with ramification index one. It is used downstream in the analysis of the Gauss valuation subring and of integral models of $X_1(Mp)$, in particular in identifying the images of the diamond automorphisms and the minimal primes of the special fibre.
